# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar Belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows how to use [SQOA Solver, a Qiskit Function by JIJ](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver), to solve a maximum independent set (MIS) problem with more binary variables than the selected QPU has qubits. The basic steps are to load an MIS instance from the [Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB)](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB) [\\[1\\]](#references), formulate it in quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) form with [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper), submit it to SQOA Solver for execution on an IBM&reg; QPU, and validate the returned solution.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menunjukkan cara menggunakan [SQOA Solver, sebuah Qiskit Function dari JIJ](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver), untuk menyelesaikan masalah maximum independent set (MIS) dengan variabel biner lebih banyak daripada jumlah qubit pada QPU yang dipilih. Langkah dasarnya: memuat instans MIS dari [Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB)](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB) [\\[1\\]](#references), merumuskannya dalam bentuk quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) dengan [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper), mengirimkannya ke SQOA Solver untuk dieksekusi pada QPU IBM&reg;, lalu memvalidasi solusi yang dikembalikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maximum independent set problem {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah maximum independent set {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An independent set is a subset of nodes in a graph such that no two selected nodes share an edge. A maximum independent set (MIS) is an independent set with the largest possible number of nodes. Applications of MIS include scheduling, resource allocation, and network design.\n"
msgstr "Independent set adalah himpunan bagian node dalam sebuah graf sehingga tidak ada dua node terpilih yang berbagi sisi. Maximum independent set (MIS) adalah independent set dengan jumlah node terbanyak. Penerapan MIS mencakup penjadwalan, alokasi sumber daya, dan perancangan jaringan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "MIS is NP-hard. In an exhaustive search, every additional node doubles the number of subsets to consider, so this approach is impractical even for moderately sized graphs. QOBLIB includes MIS as one of its ten problem classes, so it is a useful benchmark for evaluating quantum optimization workflows on real hardware.\n"
msgstr "MIS bersifat NP-hard. Dalam pencarian menyeluruh, setiap node tambahan menggandakan jumlah himpunan bagian yang harus dipertimbangkan, sehingga pendekatan ini tidak praktis bahkan untuk graf berukuran sedang. QOBLIB memasukkan MIS sebagai salah satu dari sepuluh kelas masalahnya, jadi ini adalah benchmark yang berguna untuk mengevaluasi alur kerja optimisasi kuantum pada perangkat keras sungguhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formulation {#mathematical-formulation}"
msgstr "Perumusan matematis {#mathematical-formulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given an undirected graph $G = (V, E)$, assign a binary variable $x_v$ to each node $v$:\n"
msgstr "Diberikan graf tak berarah $G = (V, E)$, tetapkan variabel biner $x_v$ untuk setiap node $v$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$x_v = 1$ if node $v$ is selected.\n"
msgstr "$x_v = 1$ jika node $v$ dipilih.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$x_v = 0$ otherwise.\n"
msgstr "$x_v = 0$ otherwise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [binary linear formulation](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_linear) maximizes the number of selected nodes while preventing both endpoints of any edge from being selected:\n"
msgstr "[Perumusan linear biner](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_linear) memaksimalkan jumlah node terpilih sambil mencegah kedua ujung sebuah sisi terpilih sekaligus:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\max_{x} \\quad & \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v \\\\\n"
"\\text{subject to} \\quad & x_v + x_w \\leq 1 && \\forall (v,w) \\in E, \\\\\n"
"& x_v \\in \\{0,1\\} && \\forall v \\in V.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\max_{x} \\quad & \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v \\\\\n"
"\\text{subject to} \\quad & x_v + x_w \\leq 1 && \\forall (v,w) \\in E, \\\\\n"
"& x_v \\in \\{0,1\\} && \\forall v \\in V.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The objective counts the selected nodes. Together, the edge constraints ensure that the selected nodes form an independent set.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi objektif menghitung node yang dipilih. Bersama-sama, batasan sisi memastikan node yang dipilih membentuk independent set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses QOBLIB's [binary unconstrained formulation](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_unconstrained), which replaces the edge constraints with quadratic penalties:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menggunakan [perumusan biner tanpa batasan](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_unconstrained) dari QOBLIB, yang mengganti batasan sisi dengan penalti kuadratik:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x \\in \\{0,1\\}^{|V|}} \\quad \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v - 2 \\sum_{(v,w) \\in E} x_v x_w.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x \\in \\{0,1\\}^{|V|}} \\quad \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v - 2 \\sum_{(v,w) \\in E} x_v x_w.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Whenever both endpoints of an edge are selected, the second term subtracts two from the objective. This penalty makes a conflicting selection less favorable than keeping either endpoint alone. The resulting objective is a QUBO, which is the input format that SQOA Solver accepts.\n"
msgstr "Setiap kali kedua ujung sebuah sisi terpilih, suku kedua mengurangi dua dari fungsi objektif. Penalti ini membuat pilihan yang bertentangan kurang menguntungkan daripada hanya memilih salah satu ujung. Fungsi objektif yang dihasilkan adalah QUBO, yaitu format input yang diterima SQOA Solver.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use SQOA Solver? {#why-use-sqoa-solver}"
msgstr "Kenapa pakai SQOA Solver? {#why-use-sqoa-solver}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many quantum optimization approaches assign one qubit to each binary variable, so the capacity of the quantum hardware can directly limit the problem size. SQOA Solver combines several reduction and hybrid-computing techniques to ease this restriction:\n"
msgstr "Banyak pendekatan optimisasi kuantum menetapkan satu qubit untuk setiap variabel biner, sehingga kapasitas perangkat keras kuantum bisa langsung membatasi ukuran masalah. SQOA Solver menggabungkan beberapa teknik reduksi dan komputasi hibrida untuk melonggarkan batasan ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**It can tackle problems with more binary variables than the QPU has qubits.** Presolve applies reduction rules that can fix variables and simplify the remaining QUBO while preserving at least one optimal solution. Empirically, presolve can also make the remaining QUBO sparser, which helps the QRAC-based encoding that follows it.\n"
msgstr "**Bisa menangani masalah dengan variabel biner lebih banyak daripada jumlah qubit pada QPU.** Presolve menerapkan aturan reduksi yang dapat menetapkan variabel dan menyederhanakan QUBO yang tersisa sambil mempertahankan setidaknya satu solusi optimal. Secara empiris, presolve juga bisa membuat QUBO yang tersisa lebih jarang (sparse), yang membantu encoding berbasis QRAC sesudahnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The solver then uses a QRAC-based encoding derived from Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[3\\]](#references) to represent multiple variables (up to three) with no direct QUBO interaction on the same qubit.\n"
msgstr "  Solver kemudian memakai encoding berbasis QRAC yang diturunkan dari Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[3\\]](#references) untuk merepresentasikan beberapa variabel (hingga tiga) tanpa interaksi QUBO langsung pada qubit yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The reductions from presolve and encoding depend on the problem structure. For example, in this tutorial, a 200-variable problem uses only 67 qubits.\n"
"* **It can be less sensitive to hardware noise.** Sample-based quantum diagonalization [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) uses the QPU to sample bitstrings but performs the diagonalization classically. This avoids repeated QPU evaluations for variational parameter updates and can reduce the impact of noise on the optimization workflow.\n"
"* **It automates the workflow from presolve through post-processing.** You provide a correctly formatted QUBO instance and select a backend. SQOA Solver then runs the whole workflow automatically. It applies presolve, maps the classical variables to a relaxed quantum problem, constructs and transpiles the sampling circuits, performs quantum sampling and classical diagonalization, rounds and refines the assignment, and reconstructs and evaluates the classical solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Reduksi dari presolve dan encoding bergantung pada struktur masalah. Misalnya, dalam tutorial ini, masalah dengan 200 variabel hanya memakai 67 qubit.\n"
"* **Bisa lebih tidak sensitif terhadap noise perangkat keras.** Sample-based quantum diagonalization [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) memakai QPU untuk mengambil sampel bitstring tetapi melakukan diagonalisasi secara klasik. Ini menghindari evaluasi QPU berulang untuk pembaruan parameter variasional dan dapat mengurangi dampak noise pada alur kerja optimisasi.\n"
"* **Mengotomatiskan alur kerja dari presolve hingga pascapemrosesan.** Anda menyediakan instans QUBO berformat benar dan memilih backend. SQOA Solver lalu menjalankan seluruh alur kerja secara otomatis. Ia menerapkan presolve, memetakan variabel klasik ke masalah kuantum terelaksasi, membangun dan men-transpile circuit sampling, melakukan sampling kuantum dan diagonalisasi klasik, membulatkan dan menyempurnakan penetapan, lalu merekonstruksi dan mengevaluasi solusi klasik.\n"

